-- title:
--   Occupancy at Γ₀(Mr) from Γ_H(Mr)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a rank-two residual Galois representation over the residue field whose base change to an algebraic closure is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $M$ be a positive integer with all prime divisors in $S$ and $p^{2}\nmid M$, and let $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ contain $p$ and consist, away from $p$, exactly of the primes where $\bar\rho$ is ramified; the further conditions linking $M$ to $S_{\min}$ (divisibility, and $q^{2}\mid M\Rightarrow q^{3}\nmid M$ away from $p$), unipotence of $\bar\rho$ on inertia at the primes of $S_{\min}$ other than $p$, and ordinarity at $p$ when $p\mid M$, are summarised here. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid M$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^{2}\neq (r+1)^{2}$ for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $r$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $r$ for it; assume weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ are spanned by their lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansions, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ to the residue field such that, for primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$, the Frobenius characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho$ is $X^{2}-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Put $L=Mr$ and let $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/L)^{\times}$ be the subgroup of units whose image in $\mathbb{Z}/r$ is $1$. Suppose given: a commutative module-finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $\mathbb{T}$ acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^{1}(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal{O})=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal{O})$; an idempotent splitting $Sp$ of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_j\in\mathfrak{m}_{j'}$ iff $j\neq j'$) and an index $i$ whose corner $e_i\cdot H^{1}$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$; and functions $t$ and $c$ on the generator type [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) (symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, $U_q$ for primes $q\mid L$, and diamonds $\langle d\rangle$, $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/L)^{\times}$) with values in $\mathbb{T}$ and in $\mathcal{O}$ respectively, subject to: every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts as an element of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}$ generated by the operators `opFamily` attached to the guarded generators (all generators except the $U_q$ with $q\nmid M$); $t(g)$ acts as `opFamily` $g$ for guarded $g$; $t(g)-c(g)\in\mathfrak{m}_i$ for guarded $g$; cofullness, namely every $v$ such that for each guarded $g$ and each $k$ some power $(t(g)-c(g))^{n}$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^{k}\cdot H^{1}$ lies in the corner; the residue of $c(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\nmid L$ outside $S$, $c(U_q)\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for $q\mid L$ with $q\mid M$, $q\neq p$, $q^{2}\mid M$, $c(U_p)$ a unit when $p\mid M$, and $c(\langle d\rangle)\equiv 1$; the corner is non-zero and the corner ring acts faithfully on it. Assume finally the level datum `LevelLE L L ⊤ H 1`. Then there exist a commutative module-finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $\mathbb{T}'$ acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^{1}(\Gamma_0(L),\mathcal{O})$, an idempotent splitting $Sp'$ with an index $i'$ whose corner is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, and a family $t'$ on [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) with values in $\mathbb{T}'$, such that $\mathbb{T}'$ acts through the $\mathcal{O}$-algebra generated by the guarded operators at level $\Gamma_0(L)$, $t'(g)$ acts as the corresponding operator for guarded $g$, $t'(g)-c(g)\in Sp'.\mathfrak{m}_{i'}$ for guarded $g$ with the very same residual scalars $c$, the corner of $e_{i'}$ is cofull in the above sense, non-zero, and is acted on faithfully by the corner ring.
--
--   This is the transfer of a residual Hecke eigensystem corner from the cohomology of $\Gamma_H(Mr)$, with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $r$, to the cohomology of $\Gamma_0(Mr)$, available because the index $r-1$ is invertible in $\mathcal{O}$ and the diamond operators are residually trivial; it is the step that brings the auxiliary level $Mr$ into the $\Gamma_0$-setting used by the level-raising argument. It feeds the subsequent results on freeness of the ordinary corner at level $Mr$, the computation of the rank of the corner submodule at the auxiliary level, and the identification of the corner ring with a local Hecke algebra.
